  "provenance": "Every number here is a starting value: textbook playing ranges and speeds written from general orchestration knowledge. The page that was meant to be the cited source (mymusictheory.com instrument ranges) could not be fetched in the session that wrote this file (host not reachable), so nothing below is quoted from a source. Pitches are SOUNDING MIDI numbers (C4 = 60), already transposed for transposing instruments. Replace a number with a measured or cited one, and say so here, before tightening a row. The orch.* rows are WARN-only except orch.range beyond `fail_over_semitones`, which is a physical impossibility rather than a taste. Calibration on the shipped example projects (26 November 2026) moved three starting values: the double bass goes down to C1 (24, the low-C extension most orchestral basses have) and the string note rates were raised, because a first draft flagged ordinary bass and ostinato writing.",
